To solve this problem, we need to determine how much Cynthia will spend on ice cream over 60 days, given that she eats one serving each night and each carton contains 15 servings at $4.00.

### Step 1: Determine how many servings Cynthia eats in 60 days
Cynthia eats 1 serving of ice cream every night, so in 60 days, she will eat:

$$
60 \text{ days} \times 1 \text{ serving/day} = 60 \text{ servings}
$$

### Step 2: Determine how many cartons she needs to buy
Each carton contains 15 servings, so the number of cartons she needs to buy is:

$$
\frac{60 \text{ servings}}{15 \text{ servings/carton}} = 4 \text{ cartons}
$$

### Step 3: Calculate the total cost
Each carton costs $4.00, so the total cost for 4 cartons is:

$$
4 \text{ cartons} \times 4.00 \text{ dollars/carton} = 16.00 \text{ dollars}
$$

### Final Answer:
$$
\boxed{16}
$$

