The problem requires determining how many 6-inch pieces can be obtained from a 4-foot wire. To solve this, it is essential to ensure that the units of measurement are consistent.

---

**Step 1: Convert the total length of the wire to inches.**  
Since 1 foot equals 12 inches, a 4-foot wire is:

$$
4 \, \text{feet} \times 12 \, \text{inches/foot} = 48 \, \text{inches}
$$

---

**Step 2: Determine how many 6-inch pieces can be cut from 48 inches.**  
To find the number of pieces, divide the total length by the length of each piece:

$$
\frac{48 \, \text{inches}}{6 \, \text{inches/piece}} = 8 \, \text{pieces}
$$

---

