Tom sails from 1 PM to 4 PM, which is a duration of:

$$
4 - 1 = 3 \text{ hours}
$$

His outbound speed is 10 miles per hour. Using the formula for distance:

$$
\text{Distance} = \text{Speed} \times \text{Time} = 10 \, \text{mph} \times 3 \, \text{hours} = 30 \, \text{miles}
$$

---

### Step 2: Calculate the Return Time

On his return trip, Tom sails at a speed of 6 miles per hour. To find out how long this takes, we use the formula:

$$
\text{Time} = \frac{\text{Distance}}{\text{Speed}} = \frac{30 \, \text{miles}}{6 \, \text{mph}} = 5 \, \text{hours}
$$

---

### Final Answer

$$
\boxed{5}
