Now, he needs to travel back. The problem says he travels back at 6 mph. So, the distance is the same, 30 miles, but his speed is slower. Therefore, time equals distance divided by speed. So, time back would be 30 miles divided by 6 mph. Let me do that calculation. 30 divided by 6 is 5. So, that would be 5 hours. Therefore, it takes him 5 hours to get back.

