Peter wants to go to the movies, and each time he goes, he spends $7 on a ticket and $7 on popcorn, totaling $14 per trip. He has a total of $42 for the week. To determine how many times he can go to the movies, we divide the total amount of money by the cost per trip:

$$
\frac{42}{14} = 3
$$

This means Peter can go to the movies 3 times. After spending all $42 on 3 trips, he will have:

$$
42 - (14 \times 3) = 42 - 42 = 0
$$

Thus, Peter can go to the movies \boxed{3} times and will have \boxed{0} dollars left. 

