Now, Peter has $42 for the week. The question is asking how many times he can go to the movies with that money. So I need to figure out how many times he can go if each time costs him $14. 

To find the number of times, I should divide the total amount of money he has by the cost per trip. That would be 42 divided by 14. Let me do that calculation. 14 times 3 is 42, right? Because 14 times 2 is 28, and 14 times 3 is 28 plus 14, which is 42. So 42 divided by 14 is 3. 

