Peter needs to calculate how many times he can go to the movies with his $42. 

Each movie visit costs a ticket of $7 and popcorn of $7, totaling $14 per visit. 

To determine how many times he can go, we divide his total amount of money by the cost per visit:

$$
\frac{42}{14} = 3
$$

Therefore, Peter can go to the movies **3** times.

$$
\boxed{3}
$$

