To find out how much money Bailey started with, we can work backwards from the total amount she had at the end of the 8 weeks.

First, we know that she received a weekly allowance of $5 for 8 weeks. So, the total amount she received in allowances is:

$$
5 \, \text{dollars/week} \times 8 \, \text{weeks} = 40 \, \text{dollars}
$$

At the end of the 8 weeks, she had a total of $100. This includes the money she started with and the money she received from her allowance. So, to find out how much money she started with, we can subtract the total amount she received in allowances from the total amount she had at the end:

$$
100 \, \text{dollars} - 40 \, \text{dollars} = 60 \, \text{dollars}
$$

Therefore, Bailey started with $\boxed{60}$ dollars.
