 5 days a week, 5 classes a day.  Saturday, 8 classes.  Each class has 15 students.  She charges $15 per student.

First, figure out how many classes she teaches in a week. She has 5 days a week with 5 classes each day, so that's 5 x 5 = 25 classes. Then on Saturday, she teaches 8 classes. So in total, 25 + 8 = 33 classes in a week.

Next, figure out how much money she makes per class. Each class has 15 students, and she charges $15 per student. So that's 15 students x $15 = $225 per class.

Then, multiply the number of classes in a week by the amount she makes per class. 33 classes x $225 = $7425.  

Therefore, Judy makes $7425 per week.

