First, let's figure out how much food is needed for the first 180 days. Since the puppy needs 1 cup of food each day for 180 days, that would be 180 days times 1 cup per day. 180 cups. Then, for the rest of the year, which is 365 - 180 = 185 days, she needs to feed the puppy 2 cups per day. So that's 185 days times 2 cups per day, which is 370 cups. Then, add that to the 180 cups to get the total amount of food needed for the first year. That would be 180 + 370 = 550 cups. Now, if one bag of dog food is 110 cups, how many bags does she need for 550 cups? Divide 550 by 110. 550 divided by 110 is 5. So, she needs 5 bags. 

