Cecilia needs to calculate the total amount of dog food required for her puppy in the first year. The first 180 days require 1 cup per day, and the remaining days (365 - 180 = 185 days) require 2 cups per day. 

1. Calculate the food for the first 180 days:
   $$
   180 \text{ days} \times 1 \text{ cup/day} = 180 \text{ cups}
   $$

2. Calculate the food for the remaining 185 days:
   $$
   185 \text{ days} \times 2 \text{ cups/day} = 370 \text{ cups}
   $$

3. Total food for the first year:
   $$
   180 \text{ cups} + 370 \text{ cups} = 550 \text{ cups}
   $$

4. Determine the number of 110-cup bags needed:
   $$
   \frac{550 \text{ cups}}{110 \text{ cups/bag}} = 5 \text{ bags}
   $$

Thus, Cecilia will use $\boxed{5}$ bags of dog food in the first year. 
