Title: Can You Solve This Math Problem? Dan Plants 3 Rose Bushes. The total number of thorns is calculated by first finding the total number of roses and then multiplying by the number of thorns per rose. 

1. Calculate the total number of roses:
   $$
   3 \text{ rose bushes} \times 25 \text{ roses per bush} = 75 \text{ roses}
   $$

2. Calculate the total number of thorns:
   $$
   75 \text{ roses} \times 8 \text{ thorns per rose} = 600 \text{ thorns}
   $$

Thus, the total number of thorns is $\boxed{600}$. 
