Harry slept 9 hours. James slept 2/3 of that, which is calculated as follows:

$$
\text{James's sleep} = \frac{2}{3} \times 9 = 6 \text{ hours}
$$

The difference in their sleep times is:

$$
9 - 6 = 3 \text{ hours}
$$

Thus, Harry slept $\boxed{3}$ hours more than James. 
